💡 Architecture Recommendation

For QGuard Messaging, I recommend the following approach:

✅ One Account per user across all platforms.
✅ One Subscription shared across all devices.
✅ Real-time Secure Chat synchronized between devices.
✅ One account-level Recovery Key used to recover the user's encryption keys on any trusted device.
✅ Separate Quantum Vaults on each device, with encrypted files remaining local and never synchronized automatically.

This architecture provides an experience comparable to modern secure messaging platforms while preserving the privacy and performance benefits of device-local encrypted storage. It also scales cleanly as you add support for iOS, macOS, Linux, web, and additional platforms in the future.